    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481-a2">

                <pb facs="1051" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg955"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2 in No.
                    195—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Duke of Tetuan to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: With reference to the latest note of
                    the legation under your worthy charge, relative to the claims of certain North
                    American citizens on account of the contribution exacted from them in the island
                    of Cuba, I have the honor, to make known to your excellency that the minister of
                    ultramar has communicated the contents of said note to the governor-general of
                    the island of Cuba, in order that the direction of the treasury may be put in
                    possession of the data relative to this affair, and in view of it, to report so
                    soon as may be what it may judge proper, or may decide them if it should be
                    possible, in strict accordance with existing laws.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity to reiterate to your excellency the assurances
                    of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Duke of</hi> TETUAN.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
